# NestFinder Real Estate Project

This project is a full-stack real-estate application with:
- React + Vite frontend
- Express + MongoDB backend
- JWT authentication
- Property listing APIs

## Main issues fixed
- Missing frontend source files were added.
- Missing backend folders (`config`, `routes`, `controllers`, `models`, `middleware`) were created.
- Server was wired to MongoDB and Express properly.
- Frontend API calls were configured with Vite proxy to the backend.
- Authentication and property endpoints were implemented.

## Start the project

1. Install dependencies:
   npm install

2. Start MongoDB locally (or use the MongoDB URI in `.env`).

3. Run the app:
   npm run dev

This starts:
- Frontend at http://localhost:5173
- Backend API at http://localhost:5001

## Environment
Copy `.env.example` to `.env` if needed and adjust values.

## API endpoints
- `POST /api/auth/register`
- `POST /api/auth/login`
- `GET /api/auth/me`
- `GET /api/properties`
- `POST /api/properties`
- `PUT /api/properties/:id`
- `DELETE /api/properties/:id`

## Database
The server uses MongoDB. If no `MONGO_URI` is provided, it falls back to:
`mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/nestfinder`

## Production build
npm run build
